Licensing scope
===============

The newly written recovery tools in scripts/, tests in tests/, and newly
written build/configuration/documentation files are
available under LICENSES/MIT-new-code.txt.

This grant does not cover recovered ESign code, original resources, extracted
metadata, or native decompiler/disassembly output. Those materials retain
their original ownership and any applicable original terms. Their presence
does not establish an open-source license for ESign or permission to relicense
its implementation. No license grant on behalf of ESign's author is made here.

Bundled open-source resource files retain their existing copyright and license
notices. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the notices inside the files themselves.

The original IPA/executable and personal signing inputs are not included in Git.
